<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's 1996 insurance premiums at 15.1 bln reais.</title>
<headline>Brazil's 1996 insurance premiums at 15.1 bln reais.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian insurance premiums in 1996 rose 7.59 percent to 15.1 billion reais ($14.2 billion) over the previous year, said state insurance watchdog Susep.</p>
<p>Susep said in a statement that car insurance accounted for 30.39 percent of all premiums, while health insurance accounted for 19.98 percent.</p>
<p>Sao Paulo state premiums totalled 7.18 billion or 47.58 percent of all premiums in 1996, followed by Rio de Janeiro state with 2.64 billion reais in premiums last year, or 17.49 percent, it added.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
